WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.590
It's Friday, and this is the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.510
Let's catch you up on everything new from Microsoft.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.310
Level up. Students will soon rehearse presentations in Learning Activities,

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.010
with Speaker Coach feedback on their delivery.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.620
Then practise again, with tips for clarity and confidence. It's due in December.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.620
For teachers,

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:38.490
Learning Zone is getting Minecraft connected lessons that match curriculum goals to Build Challenges.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.400
Launch them from Learning Zone, mix in project work,

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.070
and see who understood. It's due in February.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.420
And Microsoft now says Classroom will come to current A1 plans too,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.380
at no extra cost, next year.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.830
Teams is rolling out alt text for OneDrive images,

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:58.990
so screen readers can describe them.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.980
For school IT, Entra's Hard Deletion Protection, in preview,

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:07.350
keeps a deleted account restorable for seven days.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.260
It needs no extra licence, but once you protect an account,

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.810
you can't undo it, so choose carefully.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.660
One Autopatch policy now manages Windows,

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.890
.NET and quick machine recovery updates, each approved your way.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.050
And admins can now spot PCs with out-of-date Microsoft 365 apps,

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.890
and repair them remotely.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.090
In preview, Copilot in Fabric's Database Hub lets university data teams ask,

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.770
what should I fix first?

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.110
Studying databases?

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:44.390
Exam DP-800 earns Microsoft's SQL AI Developer certification.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.790
The fine print? If November's Windows update won't install,

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:52.390
Microsoft says affected PCs get repaired automatically.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.240
Exchange 2016 or 2019?

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.480
Microsoft says treat them as permanently vulnerable, and upgrade.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.550
After hours, for Xbox's 25th,

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:09.420
21 more original Xbox games landed on PC, 25 in all.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.010
And four originals, like Knights of the Old Republic and Conker,

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.120
get achievements for the first time.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.130
Plus Xbox Playback replays your first game,

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:23.840
top years and longest streak, until December 31.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:29.040
Practise the talk, build the lesson, guard the accounts, then play: level up.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.350
Zoom out, and it never stops shipping.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.800
Check the board: shipped today, and more on the way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.690
All of that, in one day. And it keeps on shipping.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.870
You've been watching the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.
